1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,830
If we divided everything on Earth

2
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:05,400
equally between 8 billion people,

3
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:06,490
what do you think you'd get?

4
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,570
Let's split it up!

5
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:08,940
First, the land.

6
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:10,330
Divide all the land on Earth,

7
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,790
and you'd get about 2.5 soccer fields.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,670
Trees?

9
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,460
There are about 3 trillion trees

10
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,040
on Earth.

11
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:19,610
So your share is about 375 trees.

12
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:21,320
Your very own little forest!

13
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:22,710
There are birds, too:

14
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,280
6 wild birds, and 3 chickens.

15
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:26,240
Gold?

16
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:28,010
Divide all the gold ever mined,

17
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:30,530
and you'd get about 27 grams.

18
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,140
That's almost a full ounce!

19
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:34,350
But the real surprise? Ants!

20
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,070
There are so many ants on Earth

21
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:38,200
that each of us gets about 2.5

22
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,310
million ants.

23
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,680
And the sky!

24
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,045
Even if we shared out the stars

25
00:00:42,065 --> 00:00:43,460
of the Milky Way, at least

26
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,250
12 stars would be yours.

27
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,030
So, which part of your share

28
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,020
would you want most?

29
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:49,050
Tell me in the comments!

30
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:53,490
Just imagine: 375 trees, 6 birds,

31
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:55,770
12 stars... it's all your share.

32
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:57,110
Take good care of them!
